# ── FLOW: AUTHENTICATION ────────────────────────────────────────────

# Signed in without the login page (the portal's legacy sign-in is held in the browser), the user's preferences reset
# to the defaults first
@Given "^login in application as '([^']*)'$"
    Given page login signs in as '$1' through the browser storage
    And page trade portal is displayed
    And page trade portal New Today Blotter view is visible

# The login page itself: a scenario about signing in, or signing in again after a logout
@Given "^login through the login page as '([^']*)'$"
    Given navigate to login page
    And page login signs in as '$1'
    And page trade portal is displayed
    And page trade portal New Today Blotter view is visible

@When "^(maker|checker|admin|user) is logged in to the trade portal$"
    When login in application as '$1'

@When "^user logs out and re-login$"
    When page user preference opens settings panel
    And page user preference clicks logout button
    And login through the login page as 'user'

@Then "^has access to the trade portal$"
    Then page trade portal is displayed
